Field mapping the spec did not name: FR2 says 'when an ADK event carries
an encrypted reasoning value' without naming the field. genai.Part.
ThoughtSignature is the only encrypted-reasoning-shaped thing ADK or
genai surfaces, so that is the mapping. []byte to string is base64.

Design decisions:
- Placement in history is the assistant message, per FR2's wording, even
  though the signature arrives on the thought part. The assistant turn is
  what a client echoes back, so putting it on the reasoning message would
  preserve the blob in a message the model never receives.
- Subtype is 'message' with the reasoning message id as entity id. The
  SDK's other subtype is 'tool-call', which does not apply to a thought
  part.
- Dedup on the encoded value rather than a 'seen once' flag, so a genuine
  second blob in one run still goes out. Both cases pinned by test.

